<title>FRANCE: France reports free-market wheat, barley, rye bids.</title>
<headline>France reports free-market wheat, barley, rye bids.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exporters made the following bids for refunds to export free-market grain at this week's EU tender, French cereals office ONIC said. Bids are in Ecus/tonne.</p>
<p>		     --- Dec 19 ---		 --- Dec 12---</p>
<p>		   Tonnage  Range of Bids   Tonnage    Range of Bids</p>
<p> Soft wheat    725,550    7.49-17.44    1,322,200  16.47-21.74</p>
<p> Barley	  553,000   28.49-32.46	143,600  30.49-34.26</p>
<p> Durum wheat    23,500    4.44-9.98	  34,100   4.98-14.47</p>
<p> Rye		 3,000    Not given	No bids</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
